{
  "text": "D-025 is the **Bygge Base Ring**, a Z-axis part; its record says a drawing and 3D reconstruction are present. [cite: D-025/part]\n\n**Drawing and reconstruction:** I can identify those assets as present, but they are not supplied here as viewable images or files. [cite: D-025/part]\n\nThe drawing records material **3.3315 (EN-AW 5005)**, weight **77.3 g**, and the callouts **8 × 3.4 THRU ALL**, **6.9 × 90°**, and **R115.5**. [cite: D-025/drawing/material, D-025/drawing/weight_g, D-025/drawing/callout/p1-1, D-025/drawing/callout/p1-2, D-025/drawing/callout/p1-3] The reconstructed outline is **Ø250 mm outer** and **Ø224 mm inner**; both are AI-sourced only, not yet reviewed, and may contain errors. [cite: D-025/template/outline/outer_diameter, D-025/template/outline/inner_diameter] Thickness has possible readings of **2.0 mm** or **3.0 mm**; this AI interpretation is not reviewed, and the A/B viewer is needed to distinguish them. [cite: D-025/template/thickness] The overall outline interpretation is **[undetermined: D-025/template/outline]** because it was not reliably determined from the evidence; features are **[undetermined: D-025/template/features_review]** and waiting for review.",
